From 318f7a369b3b8da4adc8fe03e795d487ee42f3a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:35:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mac/save-import: import native saves through a staged folder
 browser

Accept native folders, ZIP exports and complete single-file saves alongside
checked .dmsync backups. Exports can wrap their files one level too deep,
while stripping every single-folder level destroys legitimate slot layouts.
The native folder browser starts at the checked staged root and the player
chooses explicitly, without filename guesses or a custom directory index.

Following CatPawPrint's feedback in #2420, validate selected-root JKSV
metadata for this game's revision-1 account save, then exclude it from the
payload. Refuse unsupported records and device-save types without guessing
a mount. Keep ordinary same-named and nested files. Raw imports receive
import-time dates; full .dmsync backups retain their bytes and dates.

Replace only after clean game exit, retain recovery and rollback, and keep
the latest separate device save for raw imports. Pending imports participate
in the existing cloud-save choice report, including equal-to-base imports.

Native import/backup/restore/menu checks, 26 Mac app component tests and
6 documentation tests passed. An isolated native OOT save round trip through
a synthetic JKSV-format ZIP reached its existing slots on the Load screen;
console-exported JKSV backups and native Accept-click interaction remain
untested. No full host/iOS or five-game regression rerun is claimed.

Relative to the preceding menu dependency, implementation adds 999 lines;
the complete source patch adds 4283 and removes 95, including tests and
1929 lines of unmodified public libarchive headers. This remains a review
reference pending scope/order agreement in #2420, not an opened PR.

Front-ends: new: Mac native save imports require rebuilding the supervising launcher and host together; a host-only update leaves import disabled.
