+- **Current: save-import gameplay acceptance remains open.** A Mac user imported the Speedrun.com 100% practice export and reported no saved games after relaunch. All four downloaded files were present byte-identically under `save/100/`, while the game created fresh files at `save/`; the launcher had kept the previous save in its recovery folder. Both original wrapped downloads pass the real importer and restore into disposable data. The earlier custom-preview UI passed isolated root-selection, cancellation, recovery and device-save checks; it has since been replaced with macOS's native folder browser and explicit manual root selection, without automatic filename guesses. The general [save-folder preview and selection](../../../docs/reference/packing.md#importing-native-save-files-without-an-emulator-specific-conversion) uses no Mario-specific filename rules. These were not game runs: in-game progress after the corrected import still needs the player's check.
