diff --git a/dm/third_party/libarchive/README.md b/dm/third_party/libarchive/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..8b07ed00
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dm/third_party/libarchive/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# libarchive headers
+
+The two public C headers from libarchive, version 3.5.3 (upstream tag `v3.5.3`, `ARCHIVE_VERSION_NUMBER 3005003`), unmodified:
+
+- `archive.h` and `archive_entry.h`, the reading API `dm/host/save_import_mac.c` uses to stream a ZIP save import entry by entry.
+
+Apple's macOS SDK ships the library itself — `usr/lib/libarchive.tbd`, `/usr/lib/libarchive.2.dylib` — but no headers, so they are vendored here to compile against. The code links the SDK/system library with `-larchive` (`dm/host/Makefile`, `dm/host/tests/Makefile`); nothing here builds or bundles a libarchive of its own, and no Homebrew libarchive is used at build or run time. The public API these headers declare has been stable since long before the system library, so a binary built against them runs against the system library of every macOS the host supports. License: BSD (the notice at the bottom of `COPYING`, which the headers carry at the top of each file as well).
+
+Only the host and its native tests use this (`dm/host/save_import_mac.c`); the launcher (`dm/mac/pack_app.py`) compiles `save_backup_mac.c` without libarchive and stays independent of it.
