 The Mac [in-game menus](playing.md#mac-menus) use this same store for Console Mode and supported Frame Rate/Render Scale changes. They respect the same offered values, defaults and explicit launch overrides; with `DM_SAVED_CHOICES=0` they change only the running session. Rebuild the host and repack the launcher to add these menus to an existing app; its translated shader libraries are unchanged.
 
+The Mac **File → Import Save…** action also accepts [native save folders, ZIPs and complete single-file saves](playing.md#importing-a-save-on-the-mac), alongside `.dmsync` backups. A rebuilt host **and** launcher are required: raw imports replace only the primary save after exit, preserving a separate device save, while full backups replace both. `DM_MAC_RESTORE_DIR` and its typed request are private launcher/host coordination, not a front-end override; never write into a running game's save.
+
+The launcher creates a versioned `format` marker in its private request folder. Import stays disabled without the matching marker, including when a new host is put into an old app bundle: the older launcher could otherwise mistake a primary-only import for a full restore and delete device data. Do not update only the host binary for this feature.
+
+The Mac C `mac_save_import` API takes a `mac_save_root_picker` and its context after the scope output. Folder/ZIP imports call it on the importing thread with a fully validated private snapshot; native UI must marshal interaction to the main thread. It chooses a contained relative directory, or the whole export with an empty string; cancellation uses `ECANCELED`. Callers that deliberately retain the complete layout pass a null picker/context. Single-file saves and full backups do not require folder selection. See `dm/host/save_backup_mac.h` for ownership and failure guarantees.
+
 ### The cloud saves folder
 
 The folder a Mac app's save is synced through ([Cloud saves](settings.md#cloud-saves)) is not a row of the settings list, since a folder is none of its kinds. It has a key of its own in the same store: `cloudSaves.folder`, a string with the folder's absolute path (`defaults write org.nxnative.<title ID> cloudSaves.folder "$HOME/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/My Saves"`). Remove the key, or write an empty string, to turn cloud saves off. The app's settings window shows and changes the same key, so the player sees the folder a front end chose.
