+### Imported guest names escape legacy save migration
+
+- **Symptom:** a crafted save's case-alias metadata can move a payload outside the save folder on its next mount.
+- **Cause:** checked bundle paths did not validate the separate guest-name xattr. Legacy migration split that value on backslashes but accepted forward slashes inside a component, so a component could traverse its host parent.
+- **Fix:** the shared bundle reader and raw importer validate complete guest-name bytes, preserving valid case aliases and historical backslash-separated names. Migration validates the name before moving anything, and the component resolver independently refuses separators and traversal components. Existing legitimate old saves still migrate.
+- **Found on:** synthetic filesystem and archive fixtures during [Super Mario Bros. Wonder's import review](../../dm/games/010015100B514000/README.md#mac-routes), not a malicious save encountered in gameplay.
+
+### An explicit save import is undone by cloud synchronization
+
+- **Symptom:** an import succeeds locally, then the next start silently replaces it with a cloud save.
+- **Cause:** an imported hash equal to the last-synced base skipped reconciliation with a changed remote. Failed or raced publication also left no durable record of the player's import, so timestamp selection could later undo it.
+- **Fix:** after restore, the launcher records pending intent in `<save>.import` before publication. Pending imports always reconcile with the current cloud; a divergent remote replaces neither side without a hash-qualified player choice. The pre-launch report marks this as a conflict even when the imported bytes equal the last-synced base, so the existing launcher dialog offers that choice. Publication, parity or an explicit cloud choice settles the marker. Recording failure is reported rather than claiming protection.
+- **Found on:** synthetic multi-device and packaged-launcher fixtures during [Super Mario Bros. Wonder's import review](../../dm/games/010015100B514000/README.md#mac-routes); no installed game was launched for these checks.
 
